"Most tests should exercise a CHOSEN SUBSET of systems (a single system, a pair, or a named convocation of known systems) against minimal assets, isolated from the side effects of systems they don't name — so adding or changing an unrelated system can't break them. Keep exactly ONE big, slow integration test that runs fully-populated entities through the complete total system (execute_all_systems). This needs a test seam: a way to invoke a specific ordered subset of systems on a fixture, instead of always running the whole tick. Motivating case: the death e2e broke when player_location_sanitation_system (a brand-new, unrelated invariant) reseated a player the test assumed stationary — a subset test naming only [action, hp, death, respawn] would have been immune."